      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "The best time to replace a roof in Utah is late spring through early fall (specifically early fall / late summer), according to seasonal guides by Olympus Roofing and Utah Roofing Services .",
        "snippet_links": [
          {
            "text": "Olympus Roofing",
            "link": "https://olympusroofing.com/best-time-of-year-replace-roof-utah/"
          },
          {
            "text": "Utah Roofing Services",
            "link": "https://utahroofingservices.com/what-is-the-best-time-of-year-to-replace-a-roof-in-utah/"
          }
        ],
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "late spring through early fall"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1,
          2
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Seasonal Breakdown for Utah"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Fall (September \u2013 November / Sweet Spot):",
            "list": [
              {
                "snippet": "Why it\u2019s great: Moderate, crisp, and dry weather allows asphalt shingles to seal properly in the sun before winter arrives. You protect your home just in time for heavy Wasatch Front snow."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "The downside: Peak busy season; you need to book contractors several weeks or months in advance.",
                "reference_indexes": [
                  3,
                  4,
                  5
                ]
              }
            ],
            "reference_indexes": [
              3,
              4,
              5
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Late Spring (April \u2013 June):",
            "list": [
              {
                "snippet": "Why it\u2019s great: Temperatures sit comfortably between 40\u00b0F and 85\u00b0F (ideal for shingle thermal sealing), snow and ice have cleared out, and you get ahead of summer storm and hail seasons."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "The downside: Spring weather can be unpredictable with rain delays, and contractor demand begins to pick up.",
                "reference_indexes": [
                  3,
                  6
                ]
              }
            ],
            "reference_indexes": [
              3,
              6
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Summer (July \u2013 August):",
            "list": [
              {
                "snippet": "Why it\u2019s great: Long daylight hours mean crews finish jobs faster."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "The downside: High heat can make shingles soft and vulnerable to scuffing or granule loss from foot traffic, and schedules are packed.",
                "reference_indexes": [
                  3,
                  7
                ]
              }
            ],
            "reference_indexes": [
              3,
              7
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Winter (December \u2013 March):",
            "list": [
              {
                "snippet": "Why it\u2019s great: Lower contractor demand can mean better pricing or faster scheduling."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "The downside: Cold temperatures (below 40\u00b0F) require special cold-weather installation steps like hand-sealing shingles with roofing cement, and snow or frost can cause delays.",
                "reference_indexes": [
                  1,
                  4,
                  8
                ]
              }
            ],
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              4,
              8
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like, let me know:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "The current condition of your roof (active leaks, missing shingles, or general aging?)"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Where you live in Utah (Wasatch Front, Park City/high elevation, or southern Utah?)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "I can give you more specific advice on whether to schedule now or wait."
      }
